WEBVTT

00:00.390 --> 00:03.100
<b>When you find the thief...</b>

00:00.390 --> 00:03.100
<b>Kill them!</b>

00:00.710 --> 00:02.590
When you find the thief...

00:02.590 --> 00:03.550
Kill them!

00:04.710 --> 00:06.110
Run, now!

00:20.900 --> 00:23.700
Tanizaki, have you seen Aya?

00:23.700 --> 00:24.960
No, not at all.

00:24.960 --> 00:26.110
Damn it...

00:26.110 --> 00:29.650
Aya's run off with the source 
of the contagious ability?

00:29.650 --> 00:30.980
What is going on?

00:34.100 --> 00:35.260
Tanizaki!

00:41.580 --> 00:44.540
<i>I can't move my body very well.</i>

00:44.540 --> 00:46.370
<i>Is it because of this drug?</i>

00:47.710 --> 00:50.610
<i>I need to do something about this first.</i>

00:53.250 --> 00:55.580
Shall I scratch it with this?

02:28.510 --> 02:30.790
I do not wish to die.

02:30.790 --> 02:33.110
Not out here, in the middle of nowhere.

02:33.920 --> 02:40.050
To die neither for my country nor for my 
comrades, but as simply as an insect...

02:40.660 --> 02:44.880
Fukuchi-dono, please avenge us.

02:44.880 --> 02:46.760
Free us from regret.

02:48.410 --> 02:49.780
Please...

03:00.530 --> 03:03.070
So bringing us here 
to Atsushi was a trap.

03:03.790 --> 03:07.250
Gen'ichiro, I can't reach 
the Agency members.

03:07.250 --> 03:08.700
Is that your doing?

03:09.010 --> 03:12.210
Your men put up a good fight.

03:16.260 --> 03:18.850
Their hearts have been stopped 
using a suppressant.

03:18.850 --> 03:22.110
An electrical pulse is keeping 
their hearts beating instead.

03:22.530 --> 03:27.770
Thus, the instant I power off the device,
 your men will die.

03:29.780 --> 03:32.430
Don't look so fierce.

03:32.430 --> 03:35.790
I don't enjoy this myself.

03:37.250 --> 03:40.650
<i>We'll trap him in the booklet Poe-kun wrote.</i>

03:40.890 --> 03:44.040
<i>He can't use his special 
ability in the novel world.</i>

03:46.160 --> 03:50.630
Sorry, but I've already received a warning 
from the future about that plan.

03:54.910 --> 03:56.450
Now, what?

03:56.450 --> 03:58.160
I have yet another hostage.

03:58.710 --> 04:00.510
That makes it clear.

04:00.510 --> 04:04.760
Gen'ichiro, your objective isn't the 
destruction of the state, is it?

04:05.830 --> 04:08.460
You have a true objective beyond that.

04:08.980 --> 04:11.460
You would have no need 
for hostages otherwise.

04:11.460 --> 04:13.530
You've known me for too long.

04:14.160 --> 04:15.430
Very well.

04:15.430 --> 04:17.390
Take a guess, then.

04:17.390 --> 04:20.280
If you don't answer correctly 
within five minutes,

04:20.280 --> 04:22.900
I'll kill all the hostages.

04:23.960 --> 04:25.950
Is your nose itchy?

04:26.570 --> 04:28.790
Shall I scratch it with this?

04:35.350 --> 04:37.690
Now you can scratch it yourself.

04:39.440 --> 04:40.800
What's with the look?

04:41.160 --> 04:43.500
Did you think I was going to eat you alive?

04:44.220 --> 04:45.540
I did.

04:48.160 --> 04:51.200
The fact you saw through me 
so quickly forced me to realize...

04:51.200 --> 04:53.770
Playing the part of a 
terrorist is difficult.

04:55.090 --> 04:56.940
I was told the truth this morning.

04:57.460 --> 05:00.170
I thought I had accepted it.

05:01.260 --> 05:05.150
But come to think of it, this was my 
first time torturing someone like you.

05:05.150 --> 05:07.920
You're neither a criminal nor a villain.

05:08.740 --> 05:12.990
Just a do-gooder who would concern 
yourself with the well-being of a child.

05:14.810 --> 05:17.280
Well, there you have it.

05:17.280 --> 05:19.480
You and I are stuck waiting here

05:19.480 --> 05:23.000
until the captain completes his great plan.

05:23.940 --> 05:27.410
Kitty, do some tricks for my entertainment.

05:27.410 --> 05:29.670
I do have a trick that 
I haven't revealed yet.

05:30.820 --> 05:32.510
I can stop the terrorists.

05:32.820 --> 05:35.070
You have justice in your heart.

05:35.070 --> 05:36.380
We still have time.

05:36.380 --> 05:37.900
Let's stop the terrorists together.

05:41.410 --> 05:45.640
Speak once more of that nonsense 
and I'll mash you into a pulp.

05:47.060 --> 05:51.560
I chose by my own will to 
stand next to the captain,

05:52.030 --> 05:57.070
yet all you can say to try to 
change my mind is "justice"?

06:05.280 --> 06:06.520
Fine.

06:06.520 --> 06:09.270
Let's play a game, then.

06:09.270 --> 06:10.640
A game?

06:11.190 --> 06:15.250
I'll tell you the true goal 
of the Decay of Angels.

06:15.860 --> 06:17.620
The true goal?

06:18.020 --> 06:23.730
Your soul will be crushed, and you 
will never get up to leave this room.

06:25.090 --> 06:26.930
It's inevitable.

06:27.490 --> 06:29.180
Do you still want to hear it?

06:33.900 --> 06:36.080
You can't defeat me.

06:36.080 --> 06:39.450
You have no way to see the future as I do.

06:43.920 --> 06:46.450
I may not see the future, 
but I do see the past.

06:47.280 --> 06:49.270
We've known each other for twenty years.

06:49.770 --> 06:56.180
I know your habits, your breath, 
your sword as well as my own.

06:58.560 --> 06:59.610
Prepare yourself!

07:08.600 --> 07:09.820
Ridiculous.

07:10.710 --> 07:13.160
You never came to the battlefield with me.

07:13.160 --> 07:15.070
What do you know of me?

07:25.580 --> 07:28.040
<i>A throwing knife with a 
hundred times the power.</i>

07:29.480 --> 07:32.280
That battlefield changed everything.

07:32.280 --> 07:35.440
The man you knew is no more.

07:36.080 --> 07:40.020
You and I, as we were in those days,
 no longer exist anywhere.

07:45.280 --> 07:46.480
Who are you?

07:46.480 --> 07:47.580
Speak your name.

07:47.580 --> 07:50.020
I'm here to defeat this dojo.

07:50.830 --> 07:52.520
Thirty-nine.

07:53.750 --> 07:56.780
That's the number of dojos 
that have been stormed by you.

07:57.450 --> 08:00.120
So, where are the others?

08:00.120 --> 08:02.070
I've had them leave.

08:02.070 --> 08:02.880
What?

08:02.880 --> 08:07.870
Do you mean to say that 
you can take me on alone?

08:10.240 --> 08:11.890
Just a little boy playing with a sword...

08:12.710 --> 08:13.560
Begin!

08:23.460 --> 08:25.340
I got eighteen.

08:25.980 --> 08:29.220
How many did you get, little swordsman?

08:29.220 --> 08:31.120
Eighteen.

08:31.120 --> 08:33.010
Unbelievable.

08:33.010 --> 08:35.880
To think anyone could stand against me...

08:36.760 --> 08:38.780
I'm Fukuchi Gen'ichiro.

08:39.260 --> 08:40.250
What's your name?

08:41.160 --> 08:42.400
Fukuzawa.

08:42.750 --> 08:44.940
The way of the sword is enjoyable.

08:45.480 --> 08:47.880
The way of the sword is never lonely!

08:48.490 --> 08:51.220
Say, Fukuzawa, I've made up my mind.

08:51.790 --> 08:54.640
I'm going to master the sword alongside you.

08:54.890 --> 08:59.200
Let's share the view from 
the pinnacle together.

09:03.430 --> 09:04.770
Nineteen.

09:04.770 --> 09:07.230
That's not fair, Fukuzawa!

09:07.600 --> 09:10.730
<b>Thirteen Years Later</b>

09:20.350 --> 09:24.350
A little threatening to be an apology for 
your arriving late, don't you think, Gen'ichiro?

09:25.600 --> 09:28.040
That's what you get for drinking without me.

09:28.640 --> 09:31.220
What about your training director job?

09:31.220 --> 09:32.300
I'm skipping.

09:32.300 --> 09:33.160
Again.

09:36.620 --> 09:39.660
I'm impressed you found such 
a fine piece in this economy.

09:39.660 --> 09:41.420
Work connections.

09:41.420 --> 09:45.270
You were so quiet, people called you 
the statue with the wooden sword.

09:45.270 --> 09:46.810
But look at you now!

09:46.810 --> 09:50.020
You were uncontrollably 
rambunctious as a child,

09:50.020 --> 09:52.570
and I hear you're rising 
through the ranks now, too.

09:53.030 --> 09:53.830
Yeah.

09:54.440 --> 09:56.620
I've been tapped for a higher position.

10:01.610 --> 10:03.360
Wait, are you going to the battlefield?

10:04.070 --> 10:05.860
Tokoyamijima.

10:06.430 --> 10:08.040
I hear it's quite perilous.

10:08.510 --> 10:10.880
Several of my students have not returned.

10:11.370 --> 10:12.990
I have a bad feeling about this.

10:13.600 --> 10:15.570
That you may die?

10:15.570 --> 10:16.450
No...

10:17.020 --> 10:18.610
Worse than that.

10:23.310 --> 10:27.940
I have a feeling I may not 
be able to stay myself.

10:29.110 --> 10:30.400
Fukuzawa...

10:35.060 --> 10:36.770
Would you come with me?

10:36.770 --> 10:37.600
What?

10:38.640 --> 10:40.880
I've already put in a word.

10:40.880 --> 10:45.260
Even though you've never served, you've 
been called one of the Five Great Swords.

10:45.260 --> 10:47.320
They say they'd be more 
than happy to have you.

10:48.200 --> 10:50.180
I hate organizations.

10:50.660 --> 10:54.090
I'm suited neither for command 
nor for taking orders.

10:54.090 --> 10:55.550
But, my friend!

11:02.390 --> 11:06.560
All that exists on the battlefield 
is the act of taking life.

11:08.120 --> 11:09.290
All right.

11:11.180 --> 11:14.220
You're still the lone wolf statue 
with a wooden sword.

11:15.230 --> 11:17.140
I'm different from you.

11:17.140 --> 11:18.430
I have comrades, now.

11:19.650 --> 11:20.960
I won't ask you anymore.

11:22.450 --> 11:23.590
Gen'ichiro...

11:24.030 --> 11:28.740
To protect your friends from death and 
to end a war are two different things.

11:34.820 --> 11:37.580
I'll end the war.

11:39.210 --> 11:44.800
<b><b>And thus, the lone swordsman, 
Silver Wolf Fukuzawa, 
slew the war hawks
 within the nation, 
nudging the war
 towards its end.</b></b>

11:45.430 --> 11:51.770
<b>Meanwhile, the heroic
 Mirror Lion Fukuchi 
went to the battlefield...</b>

11:53.940 --> 11:57.980
<b>...where he became a demon of carnage.</b>

11:57.980 --> 12:00.990
Episode 59

11:57.980 --> 12:00.990
<b>Land of Inhuman 
Demons (Part 2)</b>

11:58.920 --> 12:00.260
No...

12:00.980 --> 12:03.940
That's the Decay of Angels' objective?

12:04.920 --> 12:06.400
Unbelievable...

12:06.750 --> 12:10.440
The Detective Agency knew nothing.

12:11.650 --> 12:14.120
I challenge the justness of 
the heavens' directives!

12:14.970 --> 12:17.480
So that's what he meant.

12:20.310 --> 12:22.870
Here. I've unlocked the door.

12:23.310 --> 12:24.840
Are you not escaping?

12:38.190 --> 12:39.890
I won't kill you yet.

12:40.180 --> 12:44.150
The final comedy of the 
human realm needs an audience.

12:45.450 --> 12:49.990
Chairman, have you looked through 
the documents I sent you?

12:49.990 --> 12:51.280
No...

12:51.780 --> 12:54.120
Why, Fukuchi-dono?

12:54.120 --> 12:56.210
<i>It's as it's written there.</i>

12:56.480 --> 13:00.680
<i>Unlock the One Order within five minutes.</i>

13:00.680 --> 13:05.130
<i>Otherwise, I will have the vampires 
attack the world all at once.</i>

13:05.130 --> 13:06.230
I refuse to believe it.

13:06.600 --> 13:10.470
Fukuchi-dono, you're the hero who 
has saved the world numerous times!

13:10.810 --> 13:14.190
I was inspired by you to take this office!

13:14.600 --> 13:15.810
I see...

13:15.810 --> 13:18.700
I see, now, too!

13:19.010 --> 13:22.200
This, too, is part of your grand plan
 to save the world, isn't it?

13:23.190 --> 13:24.740
What a fool.

13:25.100 --> 13:27.730
<i>But a useful foolishness.</i>

13:27.730 --> 13:33.030
<i>Even after I kill the other vile angels, 
I'll keep you by my side.</i>

13:39.490 --> 13:46.680
May I trust that you will truly abort the 
vampires' attack when I unlock the One Order?

13:48.610 --> 13:52.520
Now, these are the final 
five minutes of human history.

13:53.840 --> 13:55.190
What'll it be?

13:55.190 --> 13:56.740
A game of Go, perhaps?

13:56.740 --> 14:00.710
You told me to guess what your goal is.

14:01.730 --> 14:05.310
Is revenge your goal?

14:08.370 --> 14:11.080
For your comrades in Tokoyamijima, 
who were starved of supplies

14:11.080 --> 14:13.170
and forced to consume each other?

14:13.890 --> 14:17.540
For the men who were shot from behind by 
their superiors upon trying to surrender?

14:17.870 --> 14:21.920
For the infantrymen forced to fight 
to their deaths by healing Gifted?

14:22.470 --> 14:24.610
Against the administrators who forced orders

14:24.610 --> 14:26.890
upon their forsaken soldiers 
using rhetoric about valor?

14:27.380 --> 14:30.660
Against the Cabinet, which pushed 
its own failures of diplomacy

14:30.660 --> 14:32.480
onto those at the front lines?

14:32.880 --> 14:35.730
Against the people, who support the Cabinet 
and spectate the war with enthusiasm?

14:35.990 --> 14:43.140
You targeted the Detective Agency to 
punish me for my betrayal, didn't you?

14:45.000 --> 14:47.330
Well, I've named your objective.

14:47.820 --> 14:49.330
Free my men!

14:54.960 --> 14:56.400
Fukuzawa...

15:09.790 --> 15:11.330
You're wrong.

15:12.860 --> 15:15.810
The Decay of Angels' true goal...

15:16.220 --> 15:19.070
Is it truly right to stop them?

15:19.770 --> 15:20.880
I don't know.

15:20.880 --> 15:22.990
I can't make such a decision.

15:22.990 --> 15:25.040
Is it really that hard to know?

15:27.090 --> 15:29.050
Failure is unacceptable.

15:30.050 --> 15:32.290
You don't need to do anything.

15:43.860 --> 15:45.040
Look outside.

15:45.490 --> 15:46.650
Outside?

15:55.030 --> 15:59.210
<i>I'm too much of a fool 
to decide what's right.</i>

15:59.750 --> 16:03.940
But that's not a real reason
 for me not to act!

16:04.880 --> 16:07.180
<i>I have to tell the president!</i>

16:08.450 --> 16:10.640
<i>The president can make the right call.</i>

16:13.000 --> 16:14.140
Stand down.

16:15.540 --> 16:16.820
Let him go.

16:20.530 --> 16:22.830
Rock, paper, scissors!

16:22.830 --> 16:23.440
Rock, paper, scissors!

16:23.440 --> 16:24.240
Rock, paper, scissors!

16:24.240 --> 16:24.790
Rock, paper, scissors!

16:25.060 --> 16:27.280
Why can't I win at all?!

16:27.280 --> 16:29.390
I know your next move from 
the tension in your arm,

16:29.390 --> 16:31.870
your gaze, and the time 
between your movements.

16:31.870 --> 16:38.190
Also, I imprint your next move into your 
subconscious with subtle gestures.

16:38.680 --> 16:41.430
Thank God you were never 
a patron at the casino.

16:41.690 --> 16:43.680
It's all in the wrist.

16:43.680 --> 16:46.730
There is no superhuman-or-normie.

16:46.730 --> 16:49.350
No, you're definitely superhuman.

16:49.350 --> 16:51.660
You defeated Fyodor single-handedly.

16:52.240 --> 16:54.150
You never needed me.

16:54.630 --> 16:59.590
So why did you choose me 
over those useful tools?

17:00.020 --> 17:01.850
I have two reasons.

17:02.800 --> 17:04.790
First is Kunikida-kun.

17:07.590 --> 17:08.170
What?

17:08.170 --> 17:11.950
It's more fun doing what I do 
when there's someone around

17:11.950 --> 17:14.470
to be surprised and amused at what I do.

17:16.080 --> 17:17.650
Don't touch me!

17:17.650 --> 17:19.900
You're bullshitting me yet again!

17:20.300 --> 17:21.570
Fine!

17:22.420 --> 17:24.430
I see how it is.

17:24.740 --> 17:27.270
I'm not even worth explaining to.

17:27.670 --> 17:29.150
That's not it.

17:29.150 --> 17:33.010
I just didn't think you'd get it,
even if I did.

17:33.470 --> 17:37.990
You've been getting used by 
all sorts of organizations.

17:37.990 --> 17:40.530
You'd be hard-pressed to understand...

17:41.140 --> 17:42.200
But.

17:42.200 --> 17:43.950
Well, wanna try anyway?

17:44.980 --> 17:46.970
First, there's one thing 
I want to make sure of.

17:46.970 --> 17:50.580
Your special ability lets you access 
information, even out of a corpse.

17:51.760 --> 17:52.700
Correct?

17:54.090 --> 17:55.170
Yeah.

17:55.170 --> 17:56.720
As long as it hasn't been long since death.

17:57.190 --> 17:59.380
That's the reason I chose you.

17:59.780 --> 18:03.860
I want you to read Fyodor's 
future plans from his sunken corpse.

18:04.140 --> 18:07.760
I suspect his ability works 
on those he touches.

18:07.760 --> 18:10.600
But now that he's dead, 
it's safe to touch him.

18:11.280 --> 18:14.290
We have to discern his 
future plans from his corpse

18:14.290 --> 18:17.150
and save the Detective Agency
 at the airport.

18:17.370 --> 18:18.550
The Detective Agency?

18:19.110 --> 18:24.490
So you chose me and plotted to kill 
Fyodor before escaping the prison...

18:24.490 --> 18:26.860
All to help the Detective Agency?

18:27.120 --> 18:30.790
Well, they <i>are</i> the hand that feeds me.

18:32.720 --> 18:37.140
<i>Something I heard in the past 
suddenly rang through my head.</i>

18:37.140 --> 18:40.210
Sigma, we're done with you.

18:41.210 --> 18:44.400
Sorry, but you just aren't useful anymore.

18:45.480 --> 18:48.310
You're a mere pawn.

18:49.200 --> 18:50.350
<i>Why?</i>

18:50.350 --> 18:51.820
<i>Why now?</i>

18:55.440 --> 18:58.910
So anyway, our destination's 
at the end of this ride.

18:59.780 --> 19:00.910
What are you doing?

19:01.200 --> 19:04.160
Gotta check the circuitry, just in case.

19:05.080 --> 19:05.770
Good.

19:05.770 --> 19:06.870
No traps.

19:07.490 --> 19:09.360
And off we go!

19:10.550 --> 19:12.250
Back to what you were saying...

19:12.730 --> 19:15.800
You said you had two 
reasons for choosing me.

19:16.190 --> 19:17.860
What's the second?

19:17.860 --> 19:22.110
If I hadn't chosen you, 
Fyodor would have silenced you.

19:22.610 --> 19:25.430
That's your second reason?

19:27.780 --> 19:30.640
<i>I guess he doesn't intend 
to answer any further.</i>

19:31.540 --> 19:33.920
<i>I wanted a home.</i>

19:33.920 --> 19:36.850
<i>A home where I could live 
without being used by anyone.</i>

19:37.250 --> 19:40.620
<i>Everyone on the outside lives using others.</i>

19:41.290 --> 19:42.620
<i>But why?</i>

19:42.970 --> 19:45.590
<i>The Detective Agency isn't using Dazai.</i>

19:45.590 --> 19:48.190
<i>Dazai isn't using the Detective Agency.</i>

19:48.630 --> 19:49.820
Odd...

19:50.380 --> 19:51.750
It's taking too long.

19:54.470 --> 19:55.500
<i>Help...</i>

19:56.030 --> 19:57.320
<i>Help me...</i>

19:57.970 --> 20:01.210
<i>I have nothing to do with this.</i>

20:01.770 --> 20:04.970
I just used my time stop 
ability as I was ordered.

20:05.350 --> 20:06.790
<i>So please...</i>

20:10.750 --> 20:12.430
Now, Dazai-kun...

20:12.430 --> 20:15.450
I'm cold and wet, so I'll keep it brief.

20:15.450 --> 20:16.810
Hey!

20:16.810 --> 20:19.600
The time stop signal ceased.

20:19.600 --> 20:22.080
My accomplice must have been killed.

20:22.430 --> 20:23.660
<i>Dazai-kun.</i>

20:23.660 --> 20:26.800
To be honest, 
I'm a little surprised.

20:27.420 --> 20:29.670
Not by the flooding, though.

20:30.180 --> 20:34.530
<i>I'm surprised at the shallowness of 
your bond with the gravity manipulator.</i>

20:34.530 --> 20:37.580
<i>You didn't even know he could stop the flood.</i>

20:37.580 --> 20:38.310
What?

20:38.790 --> 20:43.000
We bent the wall rails ahead of time.

20:44.590 --> 20:47.960
It may be the sturdiest wall in the world,

20:47.960 --> 20:52.020
but its design philosophy was to ensure 
that it would be difficult to open.

20:52.830 --> 20:58.550
As a result, it was also made to 
be difficult to close once opened.

20:59.310 --> 21:03.610
The damage on the wall meant that the door 
failed to close fully, allowing water to leak.

21:03.840 --> 21:05.070
The rest was easy.

21:05.070 --> 21:07.030
We escaped through the crack.

21:07.590 --> 21:11.580
I don't think you're cut out to 
employ the gravity manipulator,

21:11.580 --> 21:13.590
being so sloppy in your thinking.

21:13.590 --> 21:17.250
He's right that that might 
have allowed him to escape...

21:17.250 --> 21:21.800
But that wouldn't have been possible if he 
hadn't known that the flood was coming.

21:22.380 --> 21:23.930
Vampires.

21:23.930 --> 21:24.470
What?

21:24.840 --> 21:30.270
He must have changed one of the guards 
into a vampire and had them lie in wait.

21:30.270 --> 21:34.550
He suspected they were coming for him 
when they stopped contacting him.

21:35.310 --> 21:39.440
The trial by flood was appropriate for me,
 seeing as I am a servant of God.

21:39.440 --> 21:43.320
But I'm rather sickly. I would be in 
real trouble if I were to fall ill.

21:43.320 --> 21:47.810
So I'll repay you with the same trial.

